  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 2.1</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">⁊ sylle mon þæt ceapgyld ðam ðe þæt yrfe age; ⁊ dǽle man þæt oðer on twa—healf ðam hundrede, healf ðam hlaforde—butan mannum; ⁊ fo se hlaford to ðam mannum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">And the value of the livestock shall be paid to its owner, and the remainder [of the thief's property]—all except his men—shall be divided in two, half [being given] to the hundred, and half to his lord who shall also take over his men.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Et reddatur ceapgildum ei cuius pecus erat (est); et reliquum dividatur in duo: dimidium hundredo, dimidium domino —preter homines, et habeat eos dominus suus.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
